put that card on the bottom of your library.)', 'Protection from Werewolves\\nHuman creatures you control have "{T}: Add one mana of any of this creature\'s colors."\\n{4}{G}{W}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control.', 'Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature you control. It gains vigilance until end of turn.\\nFlashback {W} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', "Put a +1/+1 counter on up to one target creature you control. Tap up to one target creature you don't control, and that creature doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.\\nFlashback {1}{G}{U} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)", 'Put two +1/+1 counters on target creature. It gains vigilance, trample, lifelink, indestructible, and haste until end of turn.\\nFlashback {2}{R}{W} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Reach\\nDaybound (If a player casts no spells during their own turn, it becomes night next turn.)', 'Reach\\nNightbound (If a player casts at least two spells during their own turn, it becomes day next turn.)', 'Reach\\nWhen Brood Weaver dies, create a 1/2 green Spider creature token with reach.', 'Return target card from your graveyard to your hand.\\nFlashback {4}{G} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand. Put a +1/+1 counter on up to one target Zombie you control.\\nFlashback {3}{B} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Return target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains "If this creature would die, exile it instead."\\nFlashback {3}{W}{B} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', "Return target creature to its owner's hand. If its mana value was 3 or less, scry 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put that card on the bottom of your library.)", "Return target nonland permanent to its owner's hand. If you controlled that permanent, draw a card.", 'Rockfall Vale enters the battlefield tapped unless you control two or more other lands.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {G}.', 'Sacred Fire deals 2 damage to any target and you gain 2 life.\\nFlashback {4}{R}{W} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', "Seafaring Werewolf can't be blocked.\\nWhenever Seafaring Werewolf deals combat damage to a player, draw a card.\\nNightbound (If a player casts at least two spells during their own turn, it becomes day next turn.)", 'Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle. Then if there are three or more basic land types among lands you control, scry 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put that card on the bottom of your library.)\\nFlashback {4}{G} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Shipwreck Marsh enters the battlefield tapped unless you control two or more other lands.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {B}.', "Spells can't be countered.\\nEach instant and sorcery card in your graveyard has flashback. The flashback cost is equal to that card's mana cost.", 'Surveil 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put it into your graveyard.)\\nDraw a card.', 'Surveil 3. (Look at the top three cards of your library, then put any number of them into your graveyard and the rest on top of your library in any order.)\\nFlashback {1}{U} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', "Suspicious Stowaway can't be blocked.\\nWhenever Suspicious Stowaway deals combat damage to a player, draw a card, then discard a card.\\nDaybound (If a player casts no spells during their own turn, it becomes night next turn.)", 'Tap three untapped creatures you control: Each opponent loses 1 life.', 'Tap three untapped creatures you control: Tap target creature.', 'Target creature gains deathtouch until end of turn.\\nDraw a card.', "Target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn. If it's a Human, instead it gets +3/+3 and gains indestructible until end of turn.", 'Target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.\\nCoven — Then if you control three or more creatures with different powers, draw a card.', "Target creature gets +3/+1 until end of turn. If it's your turn, that creature gains trample until end of turn. Otherwise, it gains first strike until end of turn.", "Target creature gets -2/-0 until end of turn. Create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token with decayed. (It can't block. When it attacks, sacrifice it at end of combat.)\\nDraw a card.", "Target creature gets -2/-2 until end of turn. If it's night, that creature gets -13/-13 until end of turn instead.", "Target creature you control gets +1/+1 until end of turn. It deals damage equal to its power to target creature you don't control.", 'Target creature you control gets +2/+0 and gains lifelink until end of turn. When that creature dies this turn, create a 1/1 white Spirit creature token with flying.', 'Target creature you control gets +X/+0 and gains first strike and trample until end of turn.', "Target creature's owner puts it on the top or bottom of their library. You create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token with decayed. (It can't block. When it attacks, sacrifice it at end of combat.)", "Target opponent discards two cards. You create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token with decayed. (It can't block. When it attacks, sacrifice it at end of combat.)", 'Target opponent reveals their hand. You choose a noncreature, nonland card from it. That player discards that card.', 'Target player draws two cards and loses 2 life.', 'This spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature on the battlefield.\\nDestroy all creatures.', 'This spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature that died this turn.\\nReturn target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\nFlashback {5}{B}{G} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'This spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature you attacked with this turn.\\nWhen Search Party Captain enters the battlefield, draw a card.', "This spell costs {1} less to cast if you control a Vampire.\\nNeonate's Rush deals 1 damage to target creature and 1 damage to its controller. Draw a card.", "This spell costs {2} less to cast if it's night.\\nMoonrager's Slash deals 3 damage to any target.", "Trample, haste\\nIf it's neither day nor night, it becomes day as Sunrise Cavalier enters the battlefield.\\nWhenever day becomes night or night becomes day, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature you control.", 'Trample\\nDaybound (If a player casts no spells during their own turn, it becomes night next turn.)', 'Trample\\nGrizzly Ghoul enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it for each creature that died this turn.', 'Trample\\nMounted Dreadknight enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it if an opponent lost life this turn.', 'Trample\\nNightbound (If a player casts at least two spells during their own turn, it becomes day next turn.)', 'Trample\\nOther Wolves and Werewolves you control have trample.\\n{3}{G}: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.\\nNightbound (If a player casts at least two spells during their own turn, it becomes day next turn.)', 'Trample\\nWhen Primal Adversary enters the battlefield, you may pay {1}{G} any number of times. When you pay this cost one or more times, put that many +1/+1 counters on Primal Adversary, then up to that many target lands you control become 3/3 Wolf creatures with haste that are still lands.', "Trample\\nWhenever a land card is put into your graveyard from anywhere, put a +1/+1 counter on Slogurk, the Overslime.\\nRemove three +1/+1 counters from Slogurk: Return it to its owner's hand.\\nWhen Slogurk leaves the battlefield, return up to three target land cards from your graveyard to your hand.", 'Trample\\nWhenever one or more cards leave your graveyard, put a +1/+1 counter on Willow Geist.\\nWhen Willow Geist dies, you gain life equal to its power.', 'Trample\\n{3}{G}: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.\\nDaybound (If a player casts no spells during their own turn, it becomes night next turn.)', "Up to two target creatures can't block this turn.\\nFlashback {3}{R} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)", "Vengeful Strangler can't block.\\nWhen Vengeful Strangler dies, return it to the battlefield transformed under your control attached to target creature or planeswalker an opponent controls.", "Vigilance\\nAdeline, Resplendent Cathar's power is equal to the number of creatures you control.\\nWhenever you attack, for each opponent, create a 1/1 white Human creature token that's tapped and attacking that player or a planeswalker they control.", 'Vigilance\\nCoven — At the beginning of combat on your turn, if you control three or more creatures with different powers, creatures you control get +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Vigilance\\nDaybound (If a player casts no spells during their own turn, it becomes night next turn.)', 'Vigilance\\nDisturb {3}{W} (You may cast this card from your graveyard transformed for its disturb cost.)', 'Vigilance\\nNightbound (If a player casts at least two spells during their own turn, it becomes day next turn.)', 'Vigilance\\nWhen Briarbridge Tracker enters the battlefield, investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")\\nAs long as you control a token, Briarbridge Tracker gets +2/+0.', "Voldaren Stinger has first strike as long as it's attacking.\\n{2}{R}: Voldaren Stinger gets +2/+0 until end of turn.", 'Ward {1} (Whenever this creature becomes the target of a spell or ability an opponent controls, counter it unless that player pays {1}.)\\nDaybound (If a player casts no spells during their own turn, it becomes night next turn.)', "Ward {1}\\nIf it's neither day nor night, it becomes day as Gavony Dawnguard enters the battlefield.\\nWhenever day becomes night or night becomes day, look at the top four cards of your library. You may reveal a creature card with mana value 3 or less from among them and put it into your hand. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.", 'Ward {3} (Whenever this creature becomes the target of a spell or ability an opponent controls, counter it unless that player pays {3}.)\\nNightbound (If a player casts at least two spells during their own turn, it becomes day next turn.)', 'Ward—Discard a card.\\nWhenever Graveyard Glutton enters the battlefield or attacks, exile up to two target cards from graveyards. For each creature card exiled this way, each opponent loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.\\nNightbound (If a player casts at least two spells during their own turn, it becomes day next turn.)', 'Ward—Discard a card.\\nWhenever Graveyard Trespasser enters the battlefield or attacks, exile up to one target card from a graveyard. If a creature card was exiled this way, each opponent loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.\\nDaybound (If a player casts no spells during their own turn, it becomes night next turn.)', 'When Ambitious Farmhand enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a basic Plains card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.\\nCoven — {1}{W}{W}: Transform Ambitious Farmhand. Activate only if you control three or more creatures with different powers.', 'When Ardent Elementalist enters the battlefield, return target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Arrogant Outlaw enters the battlefield, if an opponent lost life this turn, each opponent loses 2 life and you gain 2 life.', 'When Bat Whisperer enters the battlefield, if an opponent lost life this turn, create a 1/1 black Bat creature token with flying.', 'When Borrowed Time enters the battlefield, exile target nonland permanent an opponent controls until Borrowed Time leaves the battlefield.', 'When Bramble Armor enters the battlefield, attach it to target creature you control.\\nEquipped creature gets +2/+1.\\nEquip {4} ({4}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', 'When Clarion Cathars enters the battlefield, create a 1/1 white Human creature token.', "When Covert Cutpurse enters the battlefield, destroy target creature you don't control that was dealt damage this turn.\\nDisturb {4}{B} (You may cast this card from your graveyard transformed for its disturb cost.)", 'When Covetous Castaway dies, mill three cards. (Put the top three cards of your library into your graveyard.)\\nDisturb {3}{U}{U} (You may cast this card from your graveyard transformed for its disturb cost.)', 'When Crossroads Candleguide enters the battlefield, exile up to one target card from a graveyard.\\n{2}: Add one mana of any color.', 'When Dawnhart Mentor enters the battlefield, create a 1/1 white Human creature token.\\nCoven — {5}{G}: Target creature you control gets +3/+3 and gains trample until end of turn. Activate only if you control three or more creatures with different powers.', 'When Dawnhart Rejuvenator enters the battlefield, you gain 3 life.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.', "When Devoted Grafkeeper enters the battlefield, mill two cards.\\nWhenever you cast a spell from your graveyard, tap target creature you don't control.\\nDisturb {1}{W}{U} (You may cast this card from your graveyard transformed for its disturb cost.)", "When Diregraf Horde enters the battlefield, create two 2/2 black Zombie creature tokens with decayed. When you do, exile up to two target cards from graveyards. (A creature with decayed can't block. When it attacks, sacrifice it at end of combat.)", 'When Dreadhound enters the battlefield, mill three cards. (Put the top three cards of your library into your graveyard.)\\nWhenever a creature dies or a creature card is put into a graveyard from a library, each opponent loses 1 life.', "When Drownyard Amalgam enters the battlefield, target player mills three cards. (They put the top three cards of their library into their graveyard.)\\n{2}{U}: Drownyard Amalgam can't be blocked this turn.", 'When Eccentric Farmer enters the battlefield, mill three cards, then you may return a land card from your graveyard to your hand. (To mill a card, put the top card of your library into your graveyard.)', 'When Famished Foragers enters the battlefield, if an opponent lost life this turn, add {R}{R}{R}.\\n{2}{R}, Discard a card: Draw a card.', 'When Gavony Silversmith enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on each of up to two target creatures.', 'When Novice Occultist dies, you draw a card and you lose 1 life.', 'When Ominous Roost enters the battlefield or whenever you cast a spell from your graveyard, create a 1/1 blue Bird creature token with flying and "This creature can block only creatures with flying."', 'When Organ Hoarder enters the battlefield, look at the top three cards of your library, then put one of them into your hand and the rest into your graveyard.', 'When Overwhelmed Archivist enters the battlefield, draw a card, then discard a card.\\nDisturb {3}{U} (You may cast this card from your graveyard transformed for its disturb cost.)', 'When Shipwreck Sifters enters the battlefield, draw a card, then discard a card.\\nWhenever you discard a Spirit card or a card with disturb, put a +1/+1 counter on Shipwreck Sifters.', 'When Slaughter Specialist enters the battlefield, each opponent creates a 1/1 white Human creature token.\\nWhenever a creature an opponent controls dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Slaughter Specialist.', 'When The Meathook Massacre enters the battlefield, each creature gets -X/-X until end of turn.\\nWhenever a creature you control dies, each opponent loses 1 life.\\nWhenever a creature an opponent controls dies, you gain 1 life.', 'When Timberland Guide enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.', "When Tovolar's Huntmaster enters the battlefield, create two 2/2 green Wolf creature tokens.\\nDaybound (If a player casts no spells during their own turn, it becomes night next turn.)", 'When Voldaren Ambusher enters the battlefield, if an opponent lost life this turn, it deals X damage to up to one target creature or planeswalker, where X is the number of Vampires you control.', 'When a spell you control deals damage, transform Flame Channeler.', 'When another creature you control dies, transform Bereaved Survivor.', 'When this creature enters the battlefield or transforms into Brutal Cathar, exile target creature an opponent controls until this creature leaves the battlefield.\\nDaybound (If a player casts no spells during their own turn, it becomes night next turn.)', "When you cast this spell, reveal cards from the top of your library until you reveal X creature cards. Put all creature cards revealed this way into your graveyard, then put the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.\\nOld Stickfingers's power and toughness are each equal to the number of creature cards in your graveyard.", 'When you next cast an instant or sorcery spell this turn, copy that spell. You may choose new targets for the copy.\\nFlashback {1}{U}{R} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Whenever Baneblade Scoundrel becomes blocked, each creature blocking it gets -1/-1 until end of turn.\\nDaybound (If a player casts no spells during their own turn, it becomes night next turn.)', "Whenever Baneclaw Marauder becomes blocked, each creature blocking it gets -1/-1 until end of turn.\\nWhenever a creature blocking Baneclaw Marauder dies, that creature's controller loses 1 life.\\nNightbound (If a player casts at least two spells during their own turn, it becomes day next turn.)", 'Whenever Creeping Inn attacks, you may exile a creature card from your graveyard. If you do, each opponent loses X life and you gain X life, where X is the number of creature cards exiled with Creeping Inn.\\n{4}: Creeping Inn phases out.', 'Whenever Dauntless Avenger attacks, return target creature card with mana value 2 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped and attacking.', 'Whenever Falkenrath Perforator attacks, it deals 1 damage to defending player.', 'Whenever Jerren, Corrupted Bishop enters the battlefield or another nontoken Human you control dies, you lose 1 life and create a 1/1 white Human creature token.\\n{2}: Target Human you control gains lifelink until end of turn.\\nAt the beginning of your end step, if you have exactly 13 life, you may pay {4}{B}{B}. If you do, transform Jerren.', "Whenever Kessig Naturalist attacks, add {R} or {G}. Until end of turn, you don't lose this mana as steps and phases end.\\nDaybound (If a player casts no spells during their own turn, it becomes night next turn.)", "Whenever Ludevic, Necrogenius enters the battlefield or attacks, mill a card.\\n{X}{U}{U}{B}{B}, Exile X creature cards from your graveyard: Transform Ludevic. X can't be 0. Activate only as a sorcery.", "Whenever Odric's Outrider or another creature you control dies, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature you control.", 'Whenever Sludge Monster enters the battlefield or attacks, put a slime counter on up to one other target creature.\\nNon-Horror creatures with slime counters on them lose all abilities and have base power and toughness 2/2.', "Whenever Sungold Sentinel enters the battlefield or attacks, exile up to one target card from a graveyard.\\nCoven — {1}{W}: Choose a color. Sungold Sentinel gains hexproof from that color until end of turn and can't be blocked by creatures of that color this turn. Activate only if you control three or more creatures with different powers.", "Whenever Tovolar's Packleader enters the battlefield or attacks, create two 2/2 green Wolf creature tokens.\\n{2}{G}{G}: Another target Wolf or Werewolf you control fights target creature you don't control.\\nNightbound (If a player casts at least two spells during their own turn, it becomes day next turn.)", 'Whenever a Wolf or Werewolf you control deals combat damage to a player, draw a card.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if you control three or more Wolves and/or Werewolves, it becomes night. Then transform any number of Human Werewolves you control.\\nDaybound', 'Whenever a Wolf or Werewolf you control deals combat damage to a player, draw a card.\\n{X}{R}{G}: Target Wolf or Werewolf you control gets +X/+0 and gains trample until end of turn.\\nNightbound', 'Whenever a creature or enchantment enters the battlefield under your control this turn, draw a card.\\nFlashback {2}{G}{W} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Whenever a spell you control deals damage, put a flame counter on Embodiment of Flame.\\n{1}, Remove a flame counter from Embodiment of Flame: Exile the top card of your library. You may play that card this turn.', 'Whenever another Zombie enters the battlefield under your control, put a +1/+1 counter on Champion of the Perished.', 'Whenever another creature enters the battlefield under your control, you gain 1 life.\\nDisturb {1}{W} (You may cast this card from your graveyard transformed for its disturb cost.)', 'Whenever another creature you control dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Unruly Mob.', "Whenever one or more nontoken creatures die, create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token with decayed. This ability triggers only once each turn. (A creature with decayed can't block. When it attacks, sacrifice it at end of combat.)", 'Whenever one or more other creatures die, draw a card. This ability triggers only once each turn.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, Festival Crasher gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, Spellrune Howler gets +2/+2 until end of turn.\\nNightbound (If a player casts at least two spells during their own turn, it becomes day next turn.)', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, Spellrune Painter gets +1/+1 until end of turn.\\nDaybound (If a player casts no spells during their own turn, it becomes night next turn.)', "Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token with decayed. (It can't block. When it attacks, sacrifice it at end of combat.)\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if you control three or more creature tokens, you may transform Poppet Stitcher.", 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, put a charge counter on Geistflame Reservoir.\\n{1}{R}, {T}, Remove any number of charge counters from Geistflame Reservoir: It deals that much damage to any target.\\n{1}{R}, {T}: Exile the top card of your library. You may play that card this turn.', 'Whenever you sacrifice another creature, you gain 1 life and scry 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put that card on the bottom of your library.)\\n{1}, Sacrifice another creature: Fleshtaker gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Wolves and Werewolves you control have haste.\\nNightbound (If a player casts at least two spells during their own turn, it becomes day next turn.)', 'You gain 2 life, draw two cards, then discard two cards.\\nFlashback {1}{W}{U} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'You have no maximum hand size.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if you have exactly thirteen cards in your hand, you win the game.\\n{3}{U}: Draw a card.', 'You may look at the top card of your library any time.\\nYou may play lands from the top of your library.\\nCoven — As long as you control three or more creatures with different powers, you may cast creature spells from the top of your library.', '[+1]: Choose up to one target artifact, up to one target creature, and up to one target land. Untap the chosen permanents you control. Tap the chosen permanents you don\'t control. You gain 2 life.\\n[−2]: Look at the top three cards of your library. Put one of them into your hand and the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.\\n[−7]: You get an emblem with "Untap all permanents you control during each opponent\'s untap step" and "You draw a card during each opponent\'s draw step."', '[+1]: Reveal the top four cards of your library. Put all land cards revealed this way into your hand and the rest into your graveyard.\\n[0]: Put any number of land cards from your hand onto the battlefield tapped.\\n[−3]: Create a green Treefolk creature token with reach and "This creature\'s power and toughness are each equal to the number of lands you control."\\n[−8]: Return all permanent cards from your graveyard to your hand. You get an emblem with "You have no maximum hand size."', '{1}, Sacrifice Frenzied Trapbreaker: Destroy target artifact or enchantment.\\nWhenever Frenzied Trapbreaker attacks, destroy target artifact or enchantment defending player controls.\\nNightbound (If a player casts at least two spells during their own turn, it becomes day next turn.)', '{1}, Sacrifice Outland Liberator: Destroy target artifact or enchantment.\\nDaybound (If a player casts no spells during their own turn, it becomes night next turn.)', '{1}, {T}, Pay 1 life, Discard a card: Draw a card, mill a card, then put a ritual counter on Heirloom Mirror. Then if it has three or more ritual counters on it, remove them and transform it. Activate only as a sorcery.', "{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Jack-o'-Lantern: Exile up to one target card from a graveyard. Draw a card.\\n{1}, Exile Jack-o'-Lantern from your graveyard: Add one mana of any color.", '{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Moonsilver Key: Search your library for an artifact card with a mana ability or a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', '{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color.\\n{5}, {T}: Transform Mystic Skull.', '{1}, {T}: Tap target nonland permanent. Transform Chilling Chronicle.', '{1}{G}: Snarling Wolf gets +2/+2 until end of turn. Activate only once each turn.', '{1}{R}, Discard a card, Sacrifice a Vampire: Draw two cards. Activate only if an opponent lost life this turn.', '{1}{R}: Fangblade Brigand gets +1/+0 and gains first strike until end of turn.\\nDaybound (If a player casts no spells during their own turn, it becomes night next turn.)', '{1}{R}: Fangblade Eviscerator gets +1/+0 and gains first strike until end of turn.\\n{4}{R}: Creatures you control get +2/+0 until end of turn.\\nNightbound (If a player casts at least two spells during their own turn, it becomes day next turn.)', '{2}, {T}: Draw a card. Transform Mysterious Tome.', '{2}, {T}: Tap target creature.', '{2}: Stuffed Bear becomes a 4/4 green Bear artifact creature until end of turn.', '{2}{B}, Sacrifice another creature: Draw a card, then transform Ecstatic Awakener. Activate only once each turn.', '{2}{G}: Pestilent Wolf gains deathtouch until end of turn.', '{3}, {T}, Sacrifice Silver Bolt: It deals 3 damage to target creature. If a Werewolf is dealt damage this way, destroy it.', "{3}{R}: Target creature can't block this turn.", '{T}, Sacrifice Evolving Wilds: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}: Add one mana of any color.\\n{T}: Add two mana of any one color. Spend this mana only to cast spells from your graveyard.\\n{G}{U}, {T}, Exile Rootcoil Creeper: Return target card with flashback you own from exile to your hand.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: Put a soul counter on Hostile Hostel. Then if there are three or more soul counters on it, remove those counters, transform it, then untap it. Activate only as a sorcery.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Field of Ruin: Destroy target nonbasic land an opponent controls. Each player searches their library for a basic land card, puts it onto the battlefield, then shuffles.', '{T}: Add {U}. Spend this mana only to pay a disturb cost or cast an instant or sorcery spell.', '{U}, Sacrifice Malevolent Hermit: Counter target noncreature spell unless its controller pays {3}.\\nDisturb {2}{U} (You may cast this card from your graveyard transformed for its disturb cost.)']
flavor: ['"A creature of stone was never meant to fly. And I see the Ulvenwald agrees with me."\\n—Halana, Kessig ranger', '"Ah, Jerren. You\'ve been such a faithful, useful insect."', '"Aha! Yes! Now I hear it, the beautiful poetry of the lights in the sky. I must reach the moon and ask what it all means!"', '"And you were almost finished with that ritual, weren\'t you, darling? How very rude of me. To make it up to you, I\'ll send you an invitation to my wedding."', '"At least I won\'t become one of . . . those things."', '"Bah! As if I had time to preserve everything."', '"Begone, moon-cursed! These folk are no prey of yours."', '"By ancient magics, by angels\' grace, we will survive this night."', '"C\'mon, fiend. I\'ll carve you up like a Harvesttide ham."', '"Careful now. Don\'t want to get the seeds stuck to your feelers like last time."', '"Day 77: The homunculus within the crystal continues to mimic my every movement. I wonder what they are writing?"\\n—Laboratory notes of Yzlkpk', '"Do not confuse justice with mercy."\\n—Odric, Order of Saint Traft', '"Do you smell that, friends? Fear and despair."', '"Even in our darkest times, Avacyn\'s light still guides us."', '"Even steel and stone return to Ghrin-Danu in time."\\n—Katilda, Dawnhart Prime', '"Far from home, little one? I know the feeling."', '"Forget your human ancestors. You\'re part of my family now."', '"Gotcha."', '"Great Ormendahl, I kneel before you, a fragment of your will, a servant of your tyranny. I beg you, release the strength within me!"', '"Help! I\'m not a zombie! Let me out!"', '"Honorable tactics are for honorable foes. These werewolves are preying on innocent travelers. I\'ll stab them in the back while they sleep if I have to."', '"I fell to my knees. I called out to Sigarda. And then I saw my tormentors blaze with blessed sunlight."', '"I see someone tried to stop you, my pet. How delightful."\\n—Ghoulcaller Gisa', '"I was a mere cutpurse until I learned the going rate for fresh corpses."', '"If I\'m going, I\'m taking you with me!"', '"If my hypothesis is correct . . ."', '"If you hear a groaning noise in the cellar, don\'t investigate. Don\'t split up. Just lock the door and barricade it."\\n—Emili, guard captain', '"If you\'re lost in a storm, follow a gryff. They always know which way calmer waters lie."\\n—Geor, Havengul fisher', '"It has no need of wealth in the afterlife. It steals and kills purely for its own spiteful amusement."\\n—Kaya', '"It was Sigarda who lifted me from despair and gave me the strength to fight on."', '"It\'s all in the follow-through."', '"It\'s creepy out here, isn\'t it, boy? I always feel like someone\'s watching us."', '"Just hold still. I\'ll help you."', '"Keep master busy with new bits or else maybe she wonders if I\'m made of bits too."', '"Lady Anje sends her regards. I\'ll carve the rest of her message into your skin."', '"Leave behind the sorrow of this body. Be blessed, being of light."', '"Let\'s see my brother\'s stitched-up little toys compete with this."\\n—Ghoulcaller Gisa', '"Like a thousand candles fighting back the darkness, we are strongest when we stand together."', '"Like us, the morning fights for survival."', '"Madness can\'t touch a mind ignited by genius."', '"Morning light, morning light,\\nChase away the fears of night."\\n—Gavony children\'s rhyme', '"My angel is the flint, and I am her steel."', '"My little winged friends tell me which of these townsfolk are worth tasting for myself."', '"Oh, thank the angels. It\'s not a werewolf, just a regular wo—"\\n—Bruno, Ulvenwald guide, last words', '"On this night, the dark will fear us."', '"One raven is a bad omen. Two are a curse. I don\'t know what this is, but it can\'t be good."\\n—Verna, priest of Sigarda', '"Pleased to meet you, Seven."', '"Rise, my pretty thing. Why rot in the river when you can serve at my bidding?"', '"Sleep? I can sleep when I\'m dead!"', '"Speak my name thrice, and be rewarded."', '"Stensia blazes with new heat. Nephalia\'s tides are chaotic. And everywhere, this unnatural frost. The land is sending a warning."\\n—Katilda, Dawnhart Prime', '"The angels may have abandoned us, but Ghrin-Danu has not."', '"The balance of day and night is shattered. We must find the Moonsilver Key."', '"The cathars have taught me many things, but I will never forget the hard, honest work that first callused my hands."', '"There\'s nothing like a good meal to really lift the spirit."', '"This Tovolar is no brainless brute. He sends his howling minions to terrorize a village for months. Sleepless nights and fear take their toll. Only then, when morale is at its worst, does he strike."\\n—Barnes, village watch', '"Tonight, we can be anything."', '"Wait! That\'s no gryff—at least not anymore."\\n—Geor, Havengul fisher', '"We can go into the dark hand-in-hand or alone. I know which I prefer."', '"We spend our entire existence pursuing the joy of our first night\'s feast."\\n—Anje Falkenrath', '"We survived the Travails! Killer angels! Horrors from beyond the moon! Now some big werewolves think they can scare us? Let \'em try."', '"Welcome to the greatest show in Kessig!"', '"Well done, young fool, well done! Now for your reward."', '"Werewolves leave messy trails. Easy to follow. Hard to forget."', '"Werewolves leave tracks. Vampires leave wrung-out corpses. This is something else."\\n—Paulin, trapper of Somberwald', '"What has been looted can be restored. The church lives on within us."', '"When a werewolf charges, you\'ll only have time for one shot. Best make it count."\\n—Captain Eberheart', '"Wherever there is life, there is power for one who knows the old ways."', '"With Avacyn gone, I no longer knew who to pray to. Alone, I wept for a sister who would never return."', '"Works every time! Well, every time they don\'t explode, anyway."\\n—Barton, stitcher', '"You and me, we\'re not built for captivity."', '"You could see the spirits all along, couldn\'t you? Well, now I can too."', '"You have my word. You\'ll see no wolf attacks while we\'re around!"', 'A barricade only buys time. So the wealthy buy more barricades.', 'A dragon is born. A province burns.', 'A duel to first blood means something very different when a vampire is involved.', 'A few townsfolk had their suspicions, but none dared accuse him openly.', 'A few weed-choked gourd patches are all that remain of the proud, thriving farms that once blanketed the province.', "A heavy net doesn't always mean a good catch.", 'A loyal crew sticks together, even after death.', 'A soulless husk of endless hunger.', "After Uda's hat boutique in Selhoff was destroyed by werewolves, she relocated outside of town and took up a new type of sewing.", 'All across Gavony, in shuttered bedrooms and locked barns, young people seek the answers their elders failed to provide.', 'All his old grudges suddenly seemed laughably petty. So he laughed.', 'Ancient evils dwell within the burning chasm called the Ashmouth, ever ready to devour those foolish enough to travel alone.', 'As Sigarda and Sorin battled, Arlinn and Teferi recovered the key from the Markov catacombs.', 'As long as evil threatens his town, the Blessed Sleep can wait.', "As long as the sun is up, you'll only lose your purse.", "As the flames consumed the killer, his eyes remained fixed on the executioner's face, his hands twitching like angry spiders.", 'As werewolf attacks increased, brutal weapons not seen since the Travails were dusted off and put to work.', 'At the edge of night, on the cusp of winter, the allure of fire grows ever stronger.', 'Aunt and Uncle Greyfeld loved dinner guests.', 'Autonomy is only skin deep.', 'Beneath the waves, lost gods stir in their slumber.', 'Better potent than predictable.', 'Bones cracked, flesh split apart, and the screams of euphoric agony gave way to unholy laughter.', 'Brimming with power from their disrupted ritual, the Dawnhart witches lashed out at the werewolf intruders.', 'But every story ended the same way: the countryside was captured in the icy grip of winter and darkened by eternal night.', 'By the end of the festival, it was the only thing still grinning.', "Chandra, Teferi, and Arlinn sought clues to the Moonsilver Key's whereabouts while Kaya dispatched the spirits obstructing their path.", 'Charity is rare on Innistrad, but kindness is always repaid.', "Cleaning up his life's work was his afterlife's work.", "Cries of panic echo along Kessig's narrow ravines as howlpacks herd their prey.", 'Death is no impediment to dinner.', 'Devils find human dwellings to be oppressively cold, dark, and unburnt.', 'Die beneath a tree, wake up a part of it.', "Do the candleguides' heads turn to follow you as you pass, or is it merely a trick of the flickering light?", 'Drownyard floods and unnatural frost made the once peaceful boardwalk deceptively treacherous.', 'Even in death, he casts his lines, forever fishing for reasons long forgotten.', "Even within the chapel's hallowed halls, the devils' laughter pierced his prayers.", 'First darkness falls. Then it burrows in.', 'For every eye gouged out, two blinked open.', "For the more refined vampire, breaking a victim's will is far more satisfying than simply taking their blood.", 'Frog is the sincerest form of flattery.', 'From every kill, a gruesome trophy.', 'Furious to find the workshop empty, the starving vampires flew into a frenzy.', 'Geor was determined to stay out until he got a bite from something big.', "Griselbrand's defeat did not mark the end of the Skirsdag cult. They simply turned their worship to the next demon to emerge from the shadows bearing offers of power.", "He rides in agitated circles, snapping orders at servants who've long since found their peace.", "He rose from the graf for every cobbler, tanner, and fool who'd been slaughtered in the parish—and they rose and shambled after him.", "He was one masked stranger among many. Blending in was child's play.", 'Heida allowed herself a moment of satisfaction as she watched the beast fall, then turned to seek another foe. It would be a long, long night.', "Her hunger won't be sated until she's tasted every bird on Innistrad.", "Hiring an experienced wilderness guide isn't cheap, but it costs less than a search party. Or a funeral.", 'In Kessig, even celebration wears a fearsome face.', "In the adrenaline-fueled chaos, she hadn't even felt the bite.", 'In the arena, vampires set aside all pretense of honor or civilization and fight like the predators they know themselves to be.', 'In the maze-like passages of the Erdwal, a wrong turn can be fatal.', 'It conducts the souls of the righteous to their blessed rest and the spirits of the evil to justice.', 'It herds souls toward eternal torment.', 'It may have been a mistake to give them minds of their own.', 'It takes a taxidermist of unusual skill to cleanly stuff and mount a beast without severing its primal, predatory drive.', 'It waited on the barn wall for decades, forgotten, looking for the perfect opportunity.', 'It was a family reunion to die for.', 'Ivold gasped in surprise. Either a very strange insect had crawled onto one of the lenses or he was seeing geists at last!', 'Markov vampires cultivate an image of such decadent elegance that it can be easy to forget they can field a deadly fighting force.', 'More than heat and the strength of his arm, it was his faith that gave the blade its unyielding edge.', "Nature bends to the witches' call.", 'Necro-alchemists gained popular support during the Travails, when geist-fueled weapons helped defend towns against mad cultists and Eldrazi monstrosities.', 'Never again would she fear the dusk.', 'Nothing is funnier to a devil than setting someone—anyone—on fire.', 'Nothing remained but a few drifting embers and the smell of smoldering hair.', "Occasionally a skaab remembers too much of its former life. Luckily, there's an easy cure.", 'Odric took no joy in violence but neither did he mourn for the twisted things he dispatched. All that mattered were the lives he had saved.', "On Innistrad, one person's windfall usually starts with another person lying face down in the mud.", 'Passage to the abyss is free, but the return trip will cost you.', 'Revenge is a circle without end.', "Sensing a plot, Sorin raced to his grandfather's resting-crypt. But someone else had gotten there first.", 'She dispatched every challenger with a sickening snap of bone.', 'She patrols the darkness so that others can forget their worries for one bright evening.', "She won't rest until she's collected specimens of every bird on Innistrad.", "She's always willing to lend a hand. It just won't be her own.", 'Silverstreak had lost her rider, but not her instinct to help humankind.', 'Skirsdag cultists believe that the right poison "purifies" a tainted soul before it makes its way to Ormendahl.', 'So many candles. So many flammables. So little time.', "Some cathars succumbed to despair at Avacyn's unmaking. The rest redoubled their efforts to carry out her work.", 'Swirling eddies of ash hide crumbling cliffs, treacherous drops, and the slavering maws of unknown evils.', "Teferi stepped calmly into the fray. Suddenly the sun paused in the sky and the werewolves' snarls froze on their faces.", 'Terms like "safe route" and "cleared district" are a source of dark humor to the cathars who patrol the ruins of Thraben.', 'The Voldaren have begun demanding blood offerings from the villagers in their territory. Their agents arrive from the sky to collect the ceremonial bowls in eerie silence.', 'The Voldaren torture pits are so expansive that prisoners have a nasty tendency to be forgotten for years.', 'The bones of doomed ships jut out from the muck while the bones of their sailors molder below.', 'The cathars arrived at the abandoned lab to find many of the unfinished projects gnawing on one another.', 'The cathars fell like leaves as Tovolar himself joined the fray.', 'The cause remained unclear, but the fact was undeniable: nights were lengthening faster than in any autumn past.', 'The chaplain would perhaps have found some small comfort had he known that the replacement window would be named in his honor.', 'The debased remnants of the Falkenrath bloodline prowl the passes near their ruined castles.', 'The elite cathars of the Parish-Blades train in all manner of techniques designed to delay and frustrate the beasts that hunt the crossways.', "The evidence was overwhelming. Tovolar's howlpack was getting bolder, smarter, and stronger.", 'The folk of Kessig build up their courage by burning effigies of the things they fear.', 'The foulest of fowl.', 'The hunters spent the evening celebrating their kill and the rest of the night running from it.', 'The legacy of evil lives on.', 'The new hire proved more than enough to replace the three farmhands who disappeared the week before.', 'The next day, the executioner was found with ashen handprints on his throat.', 'The sound of the trumpet is both warning and comfort: it tells of approaching danger but also reminds the village folk that someone is there to stand against it.', 'The stitcher died years ago, but her dutiful assistant still keeps the laboratory well stocked.', 'The stranger spoke to no one, and the townspeople gladly returned the favor.', "The surviving militia members reunited with their fallen comrades sooner than they'd hoped.", 'The villagers pored through the old storybook, hoping that one of the tales within might hold some clue to saving the fading sun.', 'The weary travelers mistook the flickering lights for a candleguide pointing the way to Harvesttide. Their relief turned to terror as lightning lit the sky.', 'They grow up so fast.', 'Though their work is widely reviled, stitchers see themselves as being on the cutting edge of science.', "To restore the day-night balance, the Celestus mechanism's Sungold Lock must be reunited with its long-lost key.", 'Tomorrow a new village, and new victims.', "Tovolar's howl of command was too much to resist, even for Arlinn's own loyal pack.", "Tracking it isn't the hard part.", 'Travelers in the Somberwald scan the ground for werewolves and other threats, unaware of what lurks above.', 'Under the light of an unnatural moon, it walked out on legs of straw with joints of hinges ripped from the barn doors.', "When Tovolar's howl sounded from the woods, it was answered from the heart of the festival.", 'When human corpses are in short supply, stitchers get creative.', 'While the Dawnhart witches focus their magic on nature and community, other covens consort with devils and twist the elements to their will.', "Widow Weber's new scarecrow seemed to attract more crows than it scared off.", "Witch, werewolf, and cathar stood shoulder to shoulder around the Sungold Lock at the center of the ritual, ready to stop Tovolar's assault—or die trying.", 'With House Voldaren ascendant, some members of the Stromkirk line took it upon themselves to "borrow" from the blood tithes.', 'With every arm in sight broken, she turned her attention to the furniture.', 'With no guards to be seen, the cobbled streets of Gatstaf echoed with howls.', 'With the cycles of day and night unspooled, the twisted sway of the moon only grew. And grew.', 'With their usual prey scared off by werewolves, the wolves of the Ulvenwald adopted inventive new hunting techniques.', 'Wolves that feast on zombie flesh and survive carry the foul diseases of the dead wherever they roam.', "You don't have to outrun the werewolf; you only have to outrun your fellow guard."]
artist: ['Aaron Miller', 'Alayna Danner', 'Alessandra Pisano', 'Alex Brock', 'Alex Negrea', 'Alix Branwyn', 'Anastasia Ovchinnikova', 'Andrea De Dominicis', 'Andrea Radeck', 'Andreas Rocha', 'Andreas Zafiratos', 'Andrew Mar', 'Andrey Kuzinskiy', 'Andy Brase', 'Anna Christenson', 'Anna Fehr', 'Anna Steinbauer', 'Antonio Bravo', 'Antonio José Manzanedo', 'Aurore Folny', 'Bastien L. Deharme', 'Billy Christian', 'Bram Sels', 'Brent Hollowell', 'Brian Valeza', 'Brigitte Roka', 'Bryan Sola', 'Cabrol', 'Caio Monteiro', 'Campbell White', 'Caroline Gariba', 'Chris Cold', 'Chris Ostrowski', 'Chris Rahn', 'Chris Rallis', 'Chris Seaman', 'Colin Boyer', 'Craig J Spearing', 'Cristi Balanescu', 'DZO', 'Daarken', 'Dan Mumford', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'Darek Zabrocki', 'Daria Khlebnikova', 'Darren Tan', 'Dave Kendall', 'David Auden Nash', 'David Palumbo', 'David Rapoza', 'Denman Rooke', 'Deruchenko Alexander', 'Dmitry Burmak', 'Donato Giancola', 'E. M. Gist', 'Ekaterina Burmak', 'Emma Rios', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Evan Cagle', 'Evyn Fong', 'Fariba Khamseh', 'Filip Burburan', 'Forrest Imel', 'Francisco Miyara', 'Greg Opalinski', 'Grzegorz Rutkowski', 'Heonhwa Choe', 'Howard Lyon', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Igor Krstic', 'Ilse Gort', 'Irina Nordsol', 'Iris Compiet', 'Isis', 'Jake Murray', 'James Ryman', 'Jason A. Engle', 'Jason Felix', 'Jason Kang', 'Jehan Choo', 'Jesper Ejsing', 'Jodie Muir', 'Joe Slucher', 'Johan Grenier', 'Johann Bodin', 'John Di Giovanni', 'John Stanko', 'Jonas De Ro', 'Joseph Meehan', 'Josh Hass', 'Joshua Alvarado', 'Joshua Raphael', 'Josu Hernaiz', 'Justine Cruz', 'Justyna Dura', 'Kari Christensen', 'Karl Kopinski', "Kasia 'Kafis' Zielińska", 'Kekai Kotaki', 'Kev Walker', 'Khurrum', 'Kieran Yanner', 'Kim Sokol', 'Lake Hurwitz', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Leanna Crossan', 'Lie Setiawan', 'Liiga Smilshkalne', 'Livia Prima', 'Lorenzo Mastroianni', 'Lucas Graciano', 'Manuel Castañón', 'Marcela Medeiros', 'Maria Zolotukhina', 'Mark Behm', 'Marta Nael', 'Martina Fačko